WEBVTT

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.601
Tap, Read, beside a learner.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:09.791
First choose the language, English or Filipino.

00:00:09.791 --> 00:00:12.913
A learner can take the test in both languages.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:16.107
The reading tool is set by the grade.

00:00:16.107 --> 00:00:18.436
Grades one to three do the Check-in.

00:00:18.436 --> 00:00:21.993
Grades four to ten read a passage and answer questions.

00:00:21.993 --> 00:00:23.740
The tool cannot be changed.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.509
In the Check-in, the learner reads aloud one task at a time.

00:00:28.509 --> 00:00:34.067
The tasks are letters, syllables, words, phrases, sentences, and then two questions.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:36.316
Tap Start when the learner begins.

00:00:37.116 --> 00:00:41.564
Tap each item that the learner reads correctly, and it turns green.

00:00:41.564 --> 00:00:44.418
A timer runs from the moment you tap Start.

00:00:44.418 --> 00:00:47.804
Finish all the tasks, even when there are mistakes.

00:00:47.804 --> 00:00:49.596
Tap, Next task, to move on.

00:00:50.396 --> 00:00:55.597
If the learner reads Tasks one to six well, you can add an optional paragraph task.

00:00:55.597 --> 00:01:00.797
When you finish, the app shows the score and the highest task the learner mastered.

00:01:00.797 --> 00:01:01.361
Tap Save.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:05.911
For Grades four to ten, the learner reads a short passage aloud.

00:01:05.911 --> 00:01:10.247
Tap Start when the learner begins, and tap Done when the learner finishes.

00:01:11.047 --> 00:01:15.126
While the learner reads, count each reading mistake with the plus button.

00:01:15.126 --> 00:01:18.535
The app records the time, and works out the words per minute.

00:01:19.335 --> 00:01:22.186
Then ask the four questions about the passage.

00:01:22.186 --> 00:01:25.533
Tap the answers the learner gives correctly, and save.

00:01:25.533 --> 00:01:29.191
The score is half reading accuracy, and half comprehension.

00:01:29.991 --> 00:01:35.263
After the test, the app may suggest the Basic or the Plus program of ARAL-Reading.

00:01:35.263 --> 00:01:36.934
This is only a suggestion.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:39.313
You know your learner, so you decide.

00:01:40.113 --> 00:01:45.067
Remember, the posttest uses the same language and the same tool as the pretest.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:49.393
So if the learner took English, the posttest will also be in English.
